==French==
{{wikipedia|lang=fr}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|fro|nombre}}, {{m|fro|nonbre}}, from {{inh|fr|la|numerus}}, ultimately from {{der|fr|ine-pro|*nem-||to assign, allot; take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-nombre.ogg|nombre|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/nɔ̃bʁ/|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|m}}

# [[number]]

====Usage notes====
* The word '''nombre''' refers to a quantity or a mathematical concept, e.g. a number of items in a set, real numbers, complex numbers, etc., while its doublet [[numéro]] refers to a label made of digits, e.g. a rank, a jersey number, a phone number or a winning lottery number.

====See also====
* {{l|fr|numéro}}
* {{l|fr|chiffre}}

