==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈnom.bɾe/|lang=es}}
** {{rhymes|ombɾe|lang=es}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|es|n.||abbreviation}}
* {{alter|es|nonbre||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|la|nomen|nōmen, nōmine}}, from {{inh|es|ine-pro|*h₁nómn̥}}.

===Noun===
{{es-noun|m}}

# [[name]]
#: ''¿Cuál es tu '''nombre'''?'' — “What is your name?”
#: ''Mi '''nombre''' es ‘Carlos’.'' — “My name is ‘Carlos’.”
# {{lb|es|grammar}} [[noun]] (sensu lato)

====Usage notes====
In Spanish, it is a bit more common to use {{m|es|llamar|llamarse|to be called}} to indicate someone’s name:
: ''¿Cómo te llamas?'' — “What is your name?” (Literally, “What do you call yourself?”)
: ''Me llamo Carlos.'' — “My name is Carlos.” (Literally, “I call myself Carlos.”)

